; pi4FbSettle.pi4 - does the firmware's display mode settle if asked
; again after a wait?
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
;
; Booted straight from the firmware, the first DisplayInit comes back
; with a 2 x 2 surface while the physical mode is a perfectly good
; 1920 x 1080. Under U-Boot the first answer is correct, because
; something had already brought video up.
;
; The theory is that the firmware has not settled a mode at the instant
; it is first asked. This tests exactly that and nothing else: ask, wait,
; ask again, and print what each attempt returned. If the size is still
; 2 x 2 on the tenth attempt the theory is wrong and the retry the
; monitor now does is worthless.
;
; ======================================================================
;  ANSWERED, 2026-08-26. THE THEORY WAS WRONG.
; ======================================================================
; All ten attempts came back 2 x 2, over 1.8 seconds. Waiting changes
; nothing, and every retry written against the settling theory has been
; taken out of display.pi4 and out of the monitor.
;
; THE REAL CAUSE was the SHAPE of the request, not its timing.
; display.pi4 sent seven separate single-tag mailbox messages. The
; firmware accumulates the framebuffer's requested state within ONE
; property transaction and allocates against what that transaction
; accumulated, so the allocate ran against a default and handed back a
; placeholder. U-Boot sends one message carrying nine tags -
; Datasheets/pi4/uboot/v2025.01_msg.c:35-47 and :159-204 - which is
; exactly why the same code worked when U-Boot had booted the board and
; failed when the firmware had.
;
; THIS FILE IS KEPT, and not out of sentiment. It is the experiment that
; killed the wrong explanation, and a wrong explanation that dies
; without a record gets proposed again by the next person who sees a
; 2 x 2 screen. Run it after the rewrite and it should settle on attempt
; 1; if it ever needs a second attempt again, something new is going on
; and the answer is still not "wait longer".

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/uart.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/timer.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/mailbox.pi4"
; #DSP_DMA_LINKED - MANDATORY, and it must be defined BEFORE display.pi4.
; 0 = the CPU drawing path and nothing else; every procedure that would
; touch the blitter is skipped at the token level and never parsed, and
; what display.pi4 still carries is ten accessors totalling 660 bytes so
; that a program can ask whether the engine was linked and be told no.
; 1 would additionally require RaspberryPi4/Lib/dma.pi4 to be included
; ahead of display.pi4.
; display.pi4's THE DMA SEAM section has the reasoning; there is no
; default because a default in the library and a different value here
; would be a hard "Constant already defined" error.
#DSP_DMA_LINKED = 0
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/display.pi4"

Procedure.i Main()
  Define i.i
  Define rc.i

  PrintNl()
  UartWriteStr("=== does the display mode settle? ===")
  PrintNl()

  If MailboxInit() = 0
    UartWriteStr("!! mailbox")
    PrintNl()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  If DisplayStandardTags() = 0
    UartWriteStr("!! tags")
    PrintNl()
    ProcedureReturn 2
  EndIf

  For i = 0 To 9
    rc = DisplayInit(1920, 1080, 32)
    UartWriteStr("  attempt ")
    PrintDec(i + 1)
    UartWriteStr("  at t+")
    PrintDec(i * 200)
    UartWriteStr(" ms  rc ")
    PrintDec(rc)
    UartWriteStr("  ")
    PrintDec(DisplayWidth())
    UartWriteStr("x")
    PrintDec(DisplayHeight())
    UartWriteStr("  pitch ")
    PrintDec(DisplayPitch())
    PrintNl()
    UartDrain()
    If rc = 1 And DisplayWidth() >= 320
      UartWriteStr("=== settled on attempt ")
      PrintDec(i + 1)
      UartWriteStr(" ===")
      PrintNl()
      ProcedureReturn 0
    EndIf
    delay(200)
  Next

  UartWriteStr("=== never settled - the retry does not help ===")
  PrintNl()
  ProcedureReturn 3
EndProcedure
